; A polymorphic call's placeholder is pinned to the argument that
; instantiates it, for the rest of the spine and for the result.
;
; `(Some 5)` was `Option _t7`: the callee's `a` was minted fresh and
; never bound, so the result matched anything, and so did a second
; parameter sharing the variable - `(-> a a Bool)` said nothing at a
; call site, `(-> a a)` answered a placeholder, and a let-bound
; `(Some 5)` matched `(Some "x")` with no diagnostic and dereferenced
; 5 as a header under the content comparison (the QA sweep's
; refutation pass). `pinArg` (2026-08-21) replaces a minted placeholder
; parameter by the argument's type when the argument has one to offer;
; it mints nothing, and a rigid source variable is never pinned.
;
;   line 25: `(same 1 "x")` - the second `a` is `Int` by then   AX3004
;   line 26: `(strLen (idf 5))` - `(idf 5)` is `Int`            AX3004
;   line 27: a let-bound `(Some "s")` is `(Option String)`, and
;            `(+ n 1)` on its binder is refused                  AX3004
(import Str)
(:: same (-> a a Bool))
(fn (same x y) true)
(:: idf (-> a a))
(fn (idf x) x)
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (if (same 1 "x")
      (strLen (idf 5))
      (let ((o (Some "s"))) (match o ((Some n) (+ n 1)) ((None) 0)))))
